<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The update manifest Glass Tweaks reads on launch. It lives in `updates/` together
  with the release zips it names, so everything published sits in one folder.

  This file is the only thing the app fetches to find out whether there is anything
  new. It is served raw from the `main` branch, so no release API and no token is
  involved:

      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ayaan192/glasstweaksupdater/main/updates/appcast.xml

  release.ps1 writes this file, so the normal way to change it is to run that script
  rather than to edit it by hand.

  It is set to 0.2.0.0, which is the version the app is on, so a copy of the app sees
  nothing to do. Raising the version and publishing is what gives it something to do:

      1. bump <Version> in windows/app/GlassTweaks.csproj, e.g. to 0.3.0
      2. run ./release.ps1   (it reads the version from that project file)
      3. commit and push updates/appcast.xml and updates/GlassTweaks-0.3.0.zip

  The rules, all of them from AutoUpdater.NET:

    version   Required. The newest published version, in X.X.X.X form. It is compared
              against the assembly version of the running app, so it must be strictly
              higher than that for anything to happen.
    url       Required. The release zip. The app downloads this file itself.
    changelog Optional. A page to read about the release.
    mandatory The mode attribute is what makes the update run itself:
                mode="0"  show the update dialog with buttons
                mode="1"  show it without a Close button
                mode="2"  no dialog at all: download and apply on the spot
              mode="2" is what Glass Tweaks uses, because the update is meant to need no
              clicks. The app also sets this in code, so an older manifest cannot quietly
              turn the buttons back on.
    checksum  Optional, and honoured. The zip is hashed before it is unpacked, so a
              truncated or altered download is refused rather than applied.

  The zip must contain GlassTweaks.exe at its root, because it is unpacked straight over
  the install folder. release.ps1 produces it in that shape.
-->
<item>
  <version>0.2.0.0</version>
  <url>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ayaan192/glasstweaksupdater/main/updates/GlassTweaks-0.2.0.zip</url>
  <changelog>https://github.com/Ayaan192/glasstweaksupdater/releases</changelog>
  <mandatory mode="2">true</mandatory>
</item>
